Fix DiscordBM 1.16.2's zstd stream decompressor throwing on any gateway payload
that needs more output space than its first allocation guess.

decompressStreamingChunk() checks "input not fully consumed" BEFORE it checks
"output buffer is full", so the normal grow-and-continue case — ZSTD_decompressStream
stopping because the output buffer filled up — is misread as a corrupt frame and
throws DecompressionError.incompleteFrame. That throw escapes the gateway's inbound
loop, swift-websocket closes the connection with 1011/unexpectedServerError and no
reason, and DiscordBM reconnects. The first allocation is max(4096, 8 * compressed
bytes), and JSON compresses far better than 8x under zstd, so once a guild's
GUILD_CREATE payload crosses that ratio EVERY connection dies a few seconds after
READY — an endless reconnect loop that Discord answers by revoking the bot token.

Order the checks so a full output buffer means "grow and continue", and keep the
incompleteFrame guard for the case it was meant for: input left over while output
space remains.

diff --git a/Sources/DiscordGateway/ZstdDecompressorWSExtension.swift b/Sources/DiscordGateway/ZstdDecompressorWSExtension.swift
index 188948f..4cfa6b9 100644
--- a/Sources/DiscordGateway/ZstdDecompressorWSExtension.swift
+++ b/Sources/DiscordGateway/ZstdDecompressorWSExtension.swift
@@ -166,15 +166,15 @@ final class ZstdStreamingDecompressor {
                     throw DecompressionError.decompressionError(description: description)
                 }
 
+                if output.pos == output.size {
+                    return .continue(newOffset: input.pos)
+                }
+
                 if input.pos < input.size {
                     throw DecompressionError.incompleteFrame
                 }
 
-                if output.pos < output.size {
-                    return .ok
-                } else {
-                    return .continue(newOffset: input.pos)
-                }
+                return .ok
             }
         }
 
